  "tags": [],
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "9057f810-d2ac-498e-aad1-61eadc70a108",
      "name": "📌 Overview – How This Workflow Works",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -64,
        464
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 2,
        "width": 800,
        "height": 732,
        "content": "## 🏡 Real Estate Voice Agent – AI Outbound Caller with Lead Qualification & Multi-Channel Logging\n\n### How it works\nA manual trigger (or CRM webhook) starts an outbound AI voice call via Vapi. After placing the call, a Telegram notification confirms the call was placed, then a polling loop (max 3 retries with Wait nodes) checks whether the call completed — preventing hanging executions. When Vapi sends the result back via webhook, three actions fire in parallel: the raw result is logged to Google Sheets, a Telegram summary is sent, and an ops Slack alert fires. The result is then normalised into a clean data object and qualified — calls over 30 seconds with status `ended` are flagged as qualified leads. Qualified leads get logged to Airtable with a `Yes` flag, trigger a hot-lead Slack alert to the sales channel, and after a 30-second Wait node (rate limit buffer), receive a follow-up email via Gmail. Unqualified calls are still logged to Airtable for audit.\n\n### Setup steps\n1. Replace `YOUR_VAPI_API_KEY`, `YOUR_VAPI_ASSISTANT_ID`, `YOUR_VAPI_PHONE_NUMBER_ID` in the Vapi node.\n2. Connect **Telegram Bot API** → replace `YOUR_TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID` in both Telegram nodes.\n3. Connect **Slack OAuth2** → replace channel IDs in the ops alert and hot-lead alert nodes.\n4. Connect **Google Sheets OAuth2** → replace `YOUR_GOOGLE_SHEET_ID`.\n5. Connect **Airtable** → replace `YOUR_AIRTABLE_BASE_ID` and `YOUR_AIRTABLE_TABLE_ID`.\n6. Connect **Gmail OAuth2** for the follow-up email node.\n7. Set the Webhook production URL in your Vapi assistant settings.\n8. Activate webhook trigger."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "2dda64bb-3262-46eb-a9ec-f34d8f79fd74",
      "name": "Section – Call Setup & Vapi Trigger",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1040,
        512
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 996,
        "height": 520,
        "content": "## 📞 Call Setup & Vapi Trigger\nSets the customer phone number, places the call via Vapi, and immediately sends a Telegram confirmation to the agent. The call ID from Vapi's response is used downstream for status polling."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "700e80ff-09ad-4cbe-8031-2cfc150a9856",
      "name": "Section – Call Status Polling Loop",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        2064,
        512
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 1376,
        "height": 504,
        "content": "## ⏱️ Call Status Polling Loop\nWaits 2 minutes then polls Vapi's API to check whether the call has ended. If not, a Limit node caps retries at 3 and a Wait node pauses 1 minute before retrying. This prevents the workflow from hanging on unanswered calls."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "293ee044-b276-46ea-916b-b610df79d4ec",
      "name": "Section – Webhook Result & Parallel Logging",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        960,
        1360
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 1188,
        "height": 984,
        "content": "## 📥 Webhook Result & Parallel Logging\nVapi POSTs the full call result here. Three parallel outputs fire: raw result → Google Sheets, Telegram summary to agent, Slack ops alert. The data is then normalised into clean fields before qualification."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "1f1a39f0-fbb0-4f44-8625-c326ad7b5513",
      "name": "Section – Lead Qualification & Airtable CRM",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        2224,
        1216
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 928,
        "height": 584,
        "content": "## 🎯 Lead Qualification & Airtable CRM\nCalls longer than 30 seconds with status `ended` are flagged as qualified leads. Qualified leads log to Airtable with `Qualified Lead = Yes` and trigger a hot-lead Slack alert. Unqualified calls still log to Airtable with `Qualified Lead = No` for audit."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "ced9ebed-2336-4d8d-bda4-c37dc79094a4",
      "name": "Section – Hot Lead Alert & Follow-up Email",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        3184,
        1136
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 424,
        "height": 600,
        "content": "## 💌 Hot Lead Alert & Follow-up Email\nQualified leads trigger a Slack hot-lead alert to the sales channel. After a 30-second Wait node (rate limit buffer), a personalised follow-up email is sent to the lead via Gmail with the call summary and next steps."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
